# Orbital Ring wheel skin, exported from ~/Blender/Ready/OrbitalRing.blend.
#
# IMPORTANT: this file includes the Geometry Nodes detail from the Bezier circle, realised into
# a mesh via a GeometryNodeRealizeInstances node before export. The three toruses alone are only
# 9416 triangles and read as a plain grey ring -- the repeated blocks are the actual detail.
# Totals: 30548 vertices / 59328 triangles; o Torus / Torus.001 / Torus.002 / OrbitalDetails.
#
# Vertex-colour RED carries the shader material id, written as srgb_to_linear(id) so Blender's
# sRGB export round-trips to the exact values: 0.0 = metal (both toruses and GN detail),
# 0.5 = the emissive shell, 1.0 = the fabric torus. Green and blue are always zero.
# Axes: Blender NEGATIVE_Z/Y (Minecraft Y-up). UVs are the active automap layer; triangulated.
# Blender 5.3.0
# www.blender.org
